      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you can define what thrashing means without adding policy into the kernel then sure we can do that.\n\nAs we discussed before, the current issue we are facing is that lmkd gets stuck and fails to relieve memory pressure in timely manner. This issue can be tackled in two ways:\n1. Detect lmkd being stuck and try relieving memory pressure (this is what this patch is doing).\n2. Create a more generic in-kernel mechanism to detect memory thrashing and generate oom-kill (like the one you referred in https://b.corp.google.com/issues/202180814#comment1).\n\nI believe #2 would take considerable time as it has to be upstreamed. So, to mitigate lmkd getting stuck issue in the short term, I implemented solution #1 represented by this patchset. When/if we get solution #2 implemented and upstreamed then we can retire this driver-based solution. Does that explain the motivation?",
      "parentUuid": "25853192_e494d665",
